design/case/case-architecture.md:203:Other pins: U2 STAT (pin 4) not used (status read over I2C), 10 kΩ to 3V3; U2 DSEL (pin 24) R28 10 kΩ to 3V3 (Table 6-1: "Connect the DSEL to a logic rail via 10-KΩ resistor"), not read by U1; U2 QON (pin 12) to a test pad; U2 D+/D- (pins 2, 3) not connected, and J1 A6/B6/A7/B7 not connected: HVDCP_EN and MAXC_EN reset to 1 ("Enable HVDCP handshake (default)", "Enable MaxCharge handshake (default)" [DS bq25895 REG02]) and the handshake asks the adapter "to raise output voltage from 5 V to 9 V / 12 V" [DS section 8.2.3.3.1]; PMID would pass that to U5 (7 V absolute maximum [DS tps2553]) and to the ring. Without D+/D- the charger cannot see a DCP, so no handshake; U1 sets the input limit from the CC reading and also clears HVDCP_EN and MAXC_EN at start. U5 U6 then see at most the USB VBUS, inside the 5.5 V operating maximum of U6 [DS tpd4e05u06 Recommended Operating Conditions]. Whether TI allows D+/D- open: open item S5; U2 ILIM (pin 10): 260 Ω to GND gives 355 / 260 = 1.37 A typ cap [DS KILIM 320-390], register sets the working limit.
design/case/case-architecture.md:227:**Lid.** The lid is the whole top of the pebble: its outline is the base's outline, the seam is cut in the straight wall (base rim z = 37.66 mm, lid underside z = 37.96 mm: an even 0.3 mm shadow gap all round, the wall runs 0.5 mm above the seam before the top edge starts), and it is a crowned cap 3.44 mm thick at the crown. It turns on a 3.0 mm steel pin fixed in the lid (x = -7.981, y = -18.746 mm, found by the search over the seam plane in `seam_layout`: at least 0.9 mm plus the pin radius from the outline, at least 2.2 mm of lid above, clear of the well, relief and notch); the pin top is 1.3 mm under the crown, so nothing is proud of the surface, and with the lid open the pin leaves a 3.2 mm blind hole in the rim. It rides on four 0.3 mm PTFE glides fixed to the lid (one a 5.0 mm washer round the pin, three 4.0 mm discs); two 4.0 mm magnets hold it closed (base magnet under a 0.5 mm skin at x = 25.619, y = 17.254 mm; the lid magnet in the lid's underside). It swivels 100 degrees to open: the smallest angle at which the swung lid uncovers the whole well and pocket with 0.3 mm to spare (the pivot sits at the -X, -Y corner; test 4b prints the sweep). Opened, the lid is held by the pin only (friction; bench item B7). The base's rim is 0.3 mm above the block's top, so the lid is 0.600 mm from the ring when closed (test 4a, needs 0.5). There is no hold-down on the ring: the pins and the V wall hold it.
