design/ecad/case/pcb/board-notes.md:189:| Touch electrode E1 through the holder wall (bench B3; CB line 24, CA line 220: "E1 reads through a 1.97 mm LCP wall") | E1 = 3.9 x 1.15 mm front copper + back pour 4.1 x 4.6 mm, area 18.9 mm2 (CB line 24 asks 18 mm2); wall 1.97 mm (case_params.json `pin_holder` key `wall_in_front_of_E1` 1.9745); ring band 2.28 to 2.42 mm from the pin-board front face (CA line 137). Touch input: U1 pin 8 = IO4 = TOUCH4 net RING_TOUCH, wire W7 | USB to UART adapter on test pads TP3 (TXD0) and TP4 (RXD0) and GND pad TP16, the case firmware test mode that prints the raw TOUCH4 reading 100 times per second; ESP-IDF touch sensor driver (default settings) | 200 readings with the case empty, then 200 with the ring seated: the mean with the ring must exceed the mean empty by at least 3 times the peak-to-peak noise of the empty readings (start value, ours); wake from deep sleep must trigger when the ring is seated 10 of 10 times | raise the touch drive setting of the ESP-IDF touch driver (name of the setting not checked here), then average 8 readings; if still below 3 times the noise, ask for a thinner front wall (CA line 220 names the 1.97 mm as the limit) |
design/ecad/case/pcb/board-notes.md:190:| LED brightness (bench B4; CS risk 6, CA line 178) | R8 470 ohm (red), R9 150 ohm (green), R10 150 ohm (blue) from 3V3 = 3.308 V (CB lines 16, 17; CS section 1). Expected currents: red (3.308 - 2.0) / 470 = 2.8 mA; green and blue: forward voltage falls to about 2.8 V at 2 to 4 mA (our estimate from the typical 3.3 V at 20 mA in case_kb_aptf1616.pdf p.1-2), so about (3.308 - 2.8) / 150 = 3.4 mA | Firmware test mode sets one colour at a time (pin low); digital multimeter (volts, 2 V range) across R8, then R9, then R10 | across R8 1.2 to 1.4 V; across R9 and R10 0.3 to 0.7 V (2 to 4.7 mA). Visible in room light through the 1.0 mm window at 1 m for all three colours | if green or blue is too dim (voltage across R9 or R10 under 0.3 V): replace R9 / R10 by 100 ohm (current about 5 mA, within the 20 mA rating of the LED); do not go below 68 ohm |
design/ecad/case/pcb/board-notes.md:191:| Boost efficiency from the cell to VRING (bench B5; CA section 4 "boost efficiency taken as 0.85", CHECKLIST of design/case) | 0.85 at 0.1 to 0.3 A on VRING; U2 boost output 4.998 V (BOOSTV code 7, CA section 4), U5 current limit 401 mA (R5 59.0 k) | Bench supply 3.70 V in place of the cell (leads W5 +, W6 -) with a second multimeter in current mode in series on W5; load: a 22 ohm 1 W resistor between spring pins P1 (VRING) and P4 (GND) with the lid closed on a dummy ring, VRING measured with a third meter; firmware test mode that starts the boost (CHG_OTG high, VRING_EN high) | Vout 4.9 to 5.1 V; Iout = Vout / 22 = 0.227 A; Iin = Vout x Iout / (0.85 x 3.7) = 0.36 A: efficiency = (Vout x Iout) / (3.70 V x Iin) must be 0.85 or more (Iin 0.36 A or less). At 0.80 the charge count scales by 0.80 / 0.85: 13.0 to 23.5 instead of the 13.8 to 25.0 of CA section 4 | below 0.85: write the measured value into CA section 4 and recompute the charge count; below 0.70 stop: check the layout of L1 and C2/C3 first |
design/ecad/case/pcb/board-notes.md:251:PCB1 grew from 35.4 mm to 37.9 mm along the cavity: 2.5 mm, toward +y (the socket side, d negative); the antenna end did not move. Board y from -17.7 mm to +20.2 mm (case frame), 0.15 mm inside the cavity wall (case.py line 142 `CAV_YH = 20.35`). Width 23.0 mm, thickness 1.0 mm, no part on the bottom face, no height change. 16 bare copper test pads TP1 to TP16 are on the bottom face (copper only, no body, as in round 1); if "no part" is meant to include them they would have to move to the top face, which has no room.
